body:
@dsnopek the only way I can get the hash to appear in the `extension_api.json` is to add this code for `StreamPeerSocket`:

```cpp
	mappings.insert("StreamPeerSocket", {
		{ "get_status", 859471121, 1156122502 },
	});
```

which ensures the `hash_compatibility` key is included, under the `StreamPeerSocket` class:

```json
		{
			"name": "StreamPeerSocket",
			"is_refcounted": true,
			"is_instantiable": false,
			"inherits": "StreamPeer",
			"api_type": "core",
			"methods": [
				{
					"name": "get_status",
					"is_const": true,
					"is_vararg": false,
					"is_static": false,
					"is_virtual": false,
					"hash": 1156122502,
					"hash_compatibility": [
						859471121
					],
					"return_value": {
						"type": "enum::StreamPeerSocket.Status"
					}
				},
```

@dsnopek I was able to achieve compatibility for `get_status` without modifying [gdextension_special_compat_hashes.cpp](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/80a219a58ad050519a8a51b76f7f43e15accc577/core/extension/gdextension_special_compat_hashes.cpp) and using the more traditional `.compat.inc` approach.

To do so, in the `StreamPeerSocket` class definition, I declared the usual compatibility block:

```cpp
#ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED
namespace compat::StreamPeerTCP {
enum class Status;
} //namespace compat::StreamPeerTCP
#endif

class StreamPeerSocket : public StreamPeer {
	GDCLASS(StreamPeerSocket, StreamPeer);

public:
	enum Status {
		STATUS_NONE,
		STATUS_CONNECTING,
		STATUS_CONNECTED,
		STATUS_ERROR,
	};

protected:
#ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED
	compat::StreamPeerTCP::Status _get_status_compat_107954() const;
	static void _bind_compatibility_methods();
#endif
```

You'll notice a type named `namespace compat::StreamPeerTCP::Status`. I'll come back to that.

In `stream_peer_socket.compat.inc` we have:

```cpp
#ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED

namespace compat::StreamPeerTCP {
enum class Status {
	STATUS_NONE = StreamPeerSocket::STATUS_NONE,
	STATUS_CONNECTING = StreamPeerSocket::STATUS_CONNECTING,
	STATUS_CONNECTED = StreamPeerSocket::STATUS_CONNECTED,
	STATUS_ERROR = StreamPeerSocket::STATUS_ERROR,
};
}

VARIANT_ENUM_CAST(compat::StreamPeerTCP::Status);

compat::StreamPeerTCP::Status StreamPeerSocket::_get_status_compat_107954() const {
	return (compat::StreamPeerTCP::Status)get_status();
}

void StreamPeerSocket::_bind_compatibility_methods() {
	ClassDB::bind_compatibility_method(D_METHOD("get_status"), &StreamPeerSocket::_get_status_compat_107954);
}

#endif
```

The secret is in the definition of `VARIANT_ENUM_CAST`, which ultimately calls `MAKE_ENUM_TYPE_INFO`:

https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/0d267e7b1e7ac1ede02c07ea7ffc3fc8b2e8fe90/core/variant/type_info.h#L196-L205

Notice that the `m_enum` parameter is stringified in the macro and passed to `enum_qualified_name_to_class_info_name`:

```cpp
GodotTypeInfo::Internal::enum_qualified_name_to_class_info_name(String(#m_enum)));
```

Based on our declaration, the string is `conv::StreamPeerTCP::Status`, and if we review the implementation of that function:

https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/0d267e7b1e7ac1ede02c07ea7ffc3fc8b2e8fe90/core/variant/type_info.h#L185-L192

we see that it strips the namespace to only take the `StreamPeerTCP::Status` name:

```cpp
// Contains namespace. We only want the class and enum names. 
 return parts[parts.size() - 2] + "." + parts[parts.size() - 1];
```

which results in:

```
StreamPeerTCP.Status
```

And that matches our original name. The compatibility hash now matches 🥳 

> [!NOTE]
>
> We had to bind the compatibility API on the `StreamPeerSocket`, which now declares the `get_status` API, so that only a the `hash_compatibility` as included in the JSON for the `StreamPeerSocket` class:
>
> ```json
> 				{
> 					"name": "get_status",
> 					"is_const": true,
> 					"is_vararg": false,
> 					"is_static": false,
> 					"is_virtual": false,
> 					"hash": 1156122502,
> 					"hash_compatibility": [
> 						859471121
> 					],
> 					"return_value": {
> 						"type": "enum::StreamPeerSocket.Status"
> 					}
> 				},
> ```

If we did not, then the C# bindings generation fails with the following, as it tries to add the method:

```
Error: /home/runner/work/godot/godot/modules/mono/glue/GodotSharp/GodotSharp/Generated/GodotObjects/StreamPeerTcp.cs(114,16): error CS0108: 'StreamPeerTcp.GetStatus()' hides inherited member 'StreamPeerSocket.GetStatus()'. Use the new keyword if hiding was intended. [/home/runner/work/godot/godot/modules/mono/glue/GodotSharp/GodotSharp/GodotSharp.csproj]
```
